mount - attach a volume at a path

  mount hd1p1 /media/data
  mount -r sd1p1 /media/card     read-only

The volume names come from `disk`; the path must already exist as a
directory. Detach with `unmount <path>`, which flushes before letting
go.

Removable media arrive under /media by themselves, so this is for
putting one somewhere else, or for a volume that was unmounted and is
wanted back. Unmount before pulling a medium out: FAT has no journal,
and the flush is the only thing that puts written data on it.
